    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0028" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p1/pg14"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.01/3–1749:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Saigon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Abbott</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Saigon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-17T15:00:00+08:00">March 17, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>66. In conversation with Lacy,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d12-f1"/> myself, General
                        Blaizot<anchor n="2" xml:id="d12-f2"/> stated second exchange of letters Bao
                    Dai–Auriol has occurred covering many points left open original agreement. Third
                    exchange Bao Dai–Pignon being drafted will cover practical application
                    agreements including question federal services. Blaizot also stated confidential
                    parliamentary processes will be completed before arrival Bao Dai April 25.
                    Emperor will return to united independent country with all preparations made for
                    prompt transfer of authority and application of agreement. Pouched Hanoi.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d12-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Abbott</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d12-f1" n="1" xml:id="d12-f1-content">
                <p>William S. B. Lacy, Assistant Chief of the Division of Southeast Asian Affairs,
                    on a visit to Saigon.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d12-f2" n="2" xml:id="d12-f2-content">
                <p>Gen. Roger Blaizot, Commander in Chief of French Forces in the Far East.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d12-f3" n="3" xml:id="d12-f3-content">
                <p>Repeated by the Department in airgram A–267, March 18, to Paris.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
